   "text": "This is rifampicin, which I identified from the drawing and wrote out as the SMILES below.\n\n- **Aromatic core:** a naphthalene-type system carrying two OH groups, a methyl, and a fused furanone with a ketone.\n- **Spiro carbon:** it carries a methyl and is bonded to two oxygens, one in the furanone ring and one linking to the enol ether CH=CH\u2013O of the macrocycle.\n- **Hydrazone side chain:** a CH=N\u2013N bond leads to an N-methylpiperazine.\n- **Amide link:** an NH\u2013C(=O) amide connects the aromatic ring to the ansa chain.\n- **Ansa chain from the amide:** C(CH3)=CH (cis) \u2013 CH=CH (trans) \u2013 CH(CH3) \u2013 CH(OH) \u2013 CH(CH3) \u2013 CH(OH) \u2013 CH(CH3) \u2013 CH(OAc) \u2013 CH(CH3) \u2013 CH(OMe) \u2013 CH=CH\u2013O.\n\nI wrote the stereochemistry from the wedges and hashes as I read them. I cross-checked it against the commonly cited rifampicin SMILES from memory, not against a database, so the stereo descriptors are the part most worth verifying.\n\nSMILES: CO[C@H]1/C=C/O[C@@]2(C)Oc3c(C)c(O)c4c(c3C2=O)c(O)c(/C=N/N2CCN(C)CC2)c(NC(=O)/C(C)=C\\C=C\\[C@H](C)[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@H](OC(C)=O)[C@@H]1C)c4O"
